{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA551675","title":"Benzalkonium chloride effect over activated sluge","description":"As a representative of the most common type of WWTPs in Costa Rica, we selected a small size residential plant located in the city of Mora, San José (9.920687, -84.243345). From the selected plant we collected a sample of the activated sludge (4 L) from an aeration tank (4 meters deep). The sample was then transferred to a sterile amber glass container, kept at a temperature of 4 ºC, and immediately transported to the laboratory. Once in the laboratory, the sample was divided into three portions. The first portion (T1 samples) was frozen immediately and used as a baseline. The second portion (T2 samples) was homogenized, distributed in 3 aliquots of 500 mL (A, B and C) and enriched with 10 mg BAC/L. Later, the three containers enriched were incubated with aeration at a temperature of 20 ºC for 96 hours. The third portion (T3) was used as a control of the process, where it followed the same protocol as B samples except that it did not have enrichment with BAC.","center":"Universidad de Costa Rica","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2019/06/28 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN12162861","Dosed","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2015-01-13",2015,"CR","San José",3621849,"San José","probable",9.92,-84.24,"Costa Rica","activated sludge",null,null,null,"urban context stated at BioProject level only"],["SAMN12162862","Dosed","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2015-01-13",2015,"CR","San José",3621849,"San José","probable",9.92,-84.24,"Costa Rica","activated sludge",null,null,null,"urban context stated at BioProject level only"],["SAMN12162863","Dosed","probable_urban","municipal_wastewat